@startuml View Active Faults Sequence Diagram
title Figure X: Fault Detection - View & Filter Active Faults Sequence Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "FaultDetection UI" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "DiagnosticService" as Service <<Control>>
database "Supabase DB" as DB <<Database>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Navigate to Fault Detection Page
activate UI

UI -> Service : getActiveFaults()
activate Service

Service -> DB : SELECT * FROM system_faults\nWHERE status != 'Resolved'
activate DB
DB --> Service : List of active/investigating faults
deactivate DB

Service --> UI : Array of Fault objects
deactivate Service

UI -> UI : Calculate Aggregate Metrics
note right : Overall Health % = (100 - weighted_fault_score)\nActive Alert Count = faults.length

UI -> UI : Render Health Metrics & Alert Table
note right : Styles badges by Severity (High/Med/Low)\nand Status (Active/Investigating).

UI --> User : Display System Health & Active Fault List
deactivate UI

@enduml
